Hello Argus,

New season, good time for a quick safety check around the house:

1. Test smoke and carbon monoxide detectors and swap out old batteries.
2. Clean gutters and downspouts so spring rain drains away from your foundati=
on.
3. Check your sump pump before the heavy storms arrive.
4. Look over your deck and railings for loose boards or rot.
5. Store grills at least 10 feet from your home's siding.

A few minutes now can prevent a costly claim later.

Stay safe,
Great Plains Mutual
